# {{ .APP_NAME }}

A minimal Go HTTP service that embeds the SpeechKit Go client. It proxies:

- `POST /transcribe` (multipart `audio=@file.wav`, optional `language=`) to
  `POST /v1/dictation/transcribe` on your SpeechKit Server.
- `POST /assist` (JSON body) to `POST /v1/assist/process`.

This template is the starting point for any Go service that wants
SpeechKit as a library dependency rather than a standalone server.

## Prerequisites

- Go 1.24+
- A running SpeechKit Server (default `{{ .SPEECHKIT_SERVER_URL }}`)
- (optional) Bearer token if the server has `auth_mode = "bearer"`

## Configure

```sh
cp .env.example .env
# edit .env to point at your SpeechKit deployment
```

## Run

```sh
go mod tidy
go run .
```

Then:

```sh
curl -F audio=@speech.wav http://localhost:8081/transcribe
curl -X POST http://localhost:8081/assist \
  -H 'Content-Type: application/json' \
  -d '{"text":"summarize the key points"}'
```

## Where to grow this

- **Voice Agent with custom tools**: import `pkg/speechkit/agentkit`,
  build a `ToolRegistry`, and wrap a Gemini Live `voiceagent.Session`.
  See <https://speechkit.cc/llms-snippets.txt> for the full pattern.
- **Background dictation worker**: replace the synchronous handler with
  a queue (Redis, NATS, …) that posts transcripts back to your app.
- **Streaming transcripts**: subscribe to the WebSocket at
  `/v1/voiceagent/sessions/{id}/ws` for realtime conversations.
